sentences.text:
The petitioner is directed to be enlarged on bail in Crime No.53/2023 of Mudbi Police Station, Bidar district, registered for the offences punishable under Sections 376(2)(f)(i)(n), 506 of IPC and Sections 4 and 6 of POCSO Act, 2012, pending in Special Case No.5045/2023 on the file of the II Additional District and Sessions Judge Court, Bidar, sitting at Basavakalyan, subject to the following conditions:
a) The petitioner shall execute personal bond for a sum of Rs.1,00,000/- with two sureties for the likesum, to the satisfaction of the jurisdictional Court;
b) The petitioner shall appear regularly on all the dates of hearing before the Trial Court unless the Trial Court exempts his appearance for valid reasons;
NC: 2025:KHC-K:61 c) The petitioner shall not directly or indirectly threaten or tamper with the prosecution witnesses;
d) The petitioner shall not involve in similar offences in future;
e) The petitioner shall not leave the jurisdiction of the Trial Court without permission of the said Court until the case registered against him is disposed off.
Sd/-
(S.VISHWAJITH SHETTY) JUDGE AMM,SVH CT:PK Rohit vs The State Of Karnataka And Anr on 8 January, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/120649466/
4

